-- title:
--   Local fraction presentation of sections over an affine chart of a base change
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $X$ be a scheme and let $f\colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism. Let $C$ be a commutative $R$-algebra and let $\iota\colon \operatorname{Spec} C \to X$ be an open immersion with $\iota$ followed by $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R \to C$. Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $\varphi\colon R \to A$ a ring homomorphism, and form the pullback $P := X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} A$ with projections $\mathrm{pr}_1$, $\mathrm{pr}_2$; write $V := \mathrm{pr}_1^{-1}(\iota''\top)$ for the preimage of the open image of $\iota$. Let $z$ be a point of $P$ whose image under $\mathrm{pr}_1$ lies in $\iota''\top$, let $U$ be an open subset of $P$ containing $z$, and let $s \in \Gamma(P, U)$. The assertion is that there exist an open $W$ of $P$ with $z \in W$, $W \le U$ and $W \le V$, together with sections $\sigma, \tau \in \Gamma(P, V)$, each belonging to the subring of $\Gamma(P,V)$ generated by the union of the image of $C$ under $\mathrm{pr}_1^{\ast}$ composed with the chart identification $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} C) \cong C$, and the image of $A$ under $\mathrm{pr}_2^{\ast}$ on global sections restricted to $V$, such that $\tau|_W$ is a unit in $\Gamma(P, W)$ and $s|_W \cdot \tau|_W = \sigma|_W$.
--
--   This is the affine-local statement that on the chart $V \cong \operatorname{Spec}(C \otimes_R A)$ of a base change, any section of the structure sheaf near a point of $V$ becomes, after multiplication by a section that is invertible on a smaller neighbourhood, the restriction of a section lying in the subring generated by the two factors. It is used in the analysis of functions on the Deligne–Rapoport model after base change, where a germ must be exhibited as a fraction in generators coming from $C$ and from $A$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_opens_restrict_mul_eq_restrict_of_mem_closure_chart_sections.lean

